<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Position vectors and the vector between two points</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A drone sprays a shamba, flying in a straight line from \(A({@A[1]@},\,{@A[2]@},\,{@A[3]@})\) to \(B({@B[1]@},\,{@B[2]@},\,{@B[3]@})\). Coordinates are in metres, measured from a corner post O.</p><p>(a) Write the position vector of B, \(\mathbf{b} = \overrightarrow{OB}\).</p><div>\(\mathbf{b} =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Write the vector \(\overrightarrow{AB}\).</p><div>\(\overrightarrow{AB} =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The position vector of B is the journey from the origin to B, so it lists B's coordinates: \(\mathbf{b} = {@vb@}\).</p><p>(b) \(\overrightarrow{AB} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}\), end minus start: \({@vb@} - {@va@} = {@vab@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
cv3(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]],[v[3]]);
/* Design: position vectors and the vector between two points, drone context. b differs from a and from a/2 in every component, so b - a, a - b, a + b and b are all different. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Exercise D, Q2(a). */
a1: rand_with_prohib(-5,6,[0]); a2: rand_with_prohib(-5,6,[0]); a3: rand_with_prohib(-5,6,[0]);
b1: rand_with_prohib(-5,6,[0,a1,a1/2]); b2: rand_with_prohib(-5,6,[0,a2,a2/2]); b3: rand_with_prohib(-5,6,[0,a3,a3/2]);
A: [a1,a2,a3]; B: [b1,b2,b3];
va: cv3(A); vb: cv3(B); vab: vb-va;
rev: va-vb; plus: va+vb;
tw1: vab+matrix([1],[0],[0]); badm: matrix([q],[1],[2]);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>A={@A@}, B={@B@}, AB={@transpose(vab)@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors II: position vectors and the vector between two points</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.6: Write the position vector of a point and the vector AB = b - a in three dimensions as column vectors.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 2(a) in Exercise D of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: a drone context and new points in three dimensions, the position vector asked first, randomised, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
